Deep copy before mutating nested object. Few approaches:

**Modern JS (structuredClone):**
```javascript
const original = { db: { host: "localhost", port: 5432 } };
const copy = structuredClone(original);
copy.db.host = "prod.example.com";
console.log(original.db.host); // "localhost" - safe
```

**JSON method (simple, no functions/symbols):**
```javascript
const copy = JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(original));
```

**Lodash:**
```javascript
const _ = require('lodash');
const copy = _.cloneDeep(original);
```

**Manual recursive (no deps):**
```javascript
function deepCopy(obj) {
  if (obj === null || typeof obj !== 'object') return obj;
  if (obj instanceof Date) return new Date(obj);
  if (obj instanceof Array) return obj.map(deepCopy);
  if (obj instanceof Object) {
    const copy = {};
    for (let key in obj) {
      if (obj.hasOwnProperty(key)) {
        copy[key] = deepCopy(obj[key]);
      }
    }
    return copy;
  }
}

const original = { db: { host: "localhost", port: 5432 } };
const copy = deepCopy(original);
copy.db.host = "prod";
console.log(original.db.host); // "localhost"
```

**TypeScript version** (generic):
```typescript
function deepCopy<T>(obj: T): T {
  if (obj === null || typeof obj !== 'object') return obj;
  if (obj instanceof Date) return new Date(obj.getTime()) as any;
  if (obj instanceof Array) return obj.map(deepCopy) as any;
  if (obj instanceof Object) {
    const copy = {} as T;
    for (let key in obj) {
      if (obj.hasOwnProperty(key)) {
        copy[key] = deepCopy(obj[key]);
      }
    }
    return copy;
  }
  return obj;
}
```

**Pick based on needs:** `structuredClone` for modern envs, JSON method if fast + simple data, lodash if already in project, manual if want control/no deps.
